+    ``built_at`` is the ASSEMBLY clock: it advances on every run, including a Saturday rebuild of Friday's data.
+    The clocks in here are the clocks of the DATA the overview reports (valuation/basis/quote/positions/stops/
+    regime/sectors and the session identity when the read resolves one). A rebuild copies them; it never
+    re-stamps them, so a weekend page can say "built 2 min ago, data from Friday's close" truthfully.
